      "id": 1,
      "text": "Price was incorporated July 14 1892 and named after the Price River, itself named for settler William Price.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Price%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Price hosts Utah State University Eastern and its Prehistoric Museum, which houses more dinosaur fossils than any other museum in the country.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitutah.com/places-to-go/cities-and-towns/price"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Price grew around coal mining, drawing immigrants from many nations and becoming one of Utah’s most culturally diverse towns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Price%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Bryner Pioneer Museum preserves early settler artifacts and offers a glimpse into the town’s railroad and mining heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.carbon.utah.gov/explore-the-corridor/stay/communities/price/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Price Mural in the municipal building captures the town’s history in colorful artwork.",
